---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/recart-alternative';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'alternatives/recart-alternative');
const desc = description(site, 'alternatives/recart-alternative');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "What must replace Recart besides the text sender?",
    "answer": "Inventory list capture, signup routing, SMS automations, campaign operations and reporting. Confirm who will perform each task after the managed team stops."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can we keep Recart capture while changing SMS?",
    "answer": "Recart publishes a List Growth offer separately from combined List Growth and SMS. Confirm the account contract, integration and permission handoff before splitting ownership."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which replacements should we evaluate?",
    "answer": "Compare Postscript for a Shopify SMS program, Klaviyo for coordinated email and SMS work, or Omnisend for forms and recovery automation. Require each to demonstrate the functions you are replacing."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does a 14% code cost on the retained cart?",
    "answer": "A $668 basket at 32% gross margin has fixed goods cost of $454.24. A 14% code reduces gross profit from $213.76 to $120.24, a loss of $93.52 before other costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16 container">
<a href="/alternatives" class="link">← All alternatives</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Recart alternatives: replace the capture and service workflow</h1>
<p class="mt-6 text-xl">Map what the managed team does before choosing a new SMS sender. You may need a service replacement, a capture replacement, or only a different channel arrangement.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-10">
<h2>Separate the scopes in the current account</h2>
<p>Sources checked November 25, 2026. Recart’s <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/recart">Shopify listing</a> describes SMS marketing, email/text list growth and automations. Email capture is a different function from sending an email recovery journey. Inventory where each captured email goes and which system owns its follow-up.</p>
<p>The <a href="https://recart.com/sms-marketing-pricing-ecommerce">current pricing page</a> separates List Growth from List Growth plus SMS, with commitment periods and usage charges. Its <a href="https://recart.com/fully-managed-sms">managed-service page</a> describes popup design, campaign work, testing and reporting, with plan-specific inclusion. Confirm the actual contract and service responsibilities; neither an app install nor a broad marketing headline defines your account scope.</p>
<p>Before ending service, obtain a list of live signup units, campaigns awaiting approval, scheduled sends, integrations and recurring reports. Give every item a new owner and request the final permission/suppression export and account-specific number-transfer process. Keep access until the receiving team has accepted the handoff. Do not assume a cancellation date is a completed migration date.</p>
<h2>Choose an alternative for the work you want to own</h2>
<p><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/postscript-sms-marketing">Postscript</a> lists SMS, RCS and email. Evaluate it when you want to operate a Shopify messaging program and need its actual flow and reply workflow demonstrated. Confirm channel access and service inclusion rather than assuming its platform contract replaces Recart’s ongoing campaign work.</p>
<p><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/klaviyo-email-marketing">Klaviyo</a> lists email, SMS and WhatsApp. It is a candidate when your existing email team wants to coordinate the SMS journey in one environment. The acceptance brief should include the capture source and the point where a purchase stops both channel queues. Budget the work to rebuild that coordination.</p>
<p><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/omnisend">Omnisend</a> lists signup forms and abandoned-cart automation alongside email and SMS. Evaluate it when the team wants to maintain capture and recovery together. Compare a real mobile form and cart journey with your present setup, including destinations and fees. None of these supplier descriptions proves a universal winner.</p>
<p>If Recart capture works but the SMS operating model does not, ask about retaining the List Growth scope and routing to the chosen sender. Conversely, changing an email provider alone may leave the Recart SMS arrangement useful. Obtain a supported integration and field map before committing to either split; no automatic suppression sharing is assumed.</p>
<h2>Acceptance cases for a capture-and-service handoff</h2>
<h3>A mobile signup reaches the wrong channel</h3>
<p>Recart’s <a href="https://recart.com/oneclick">OneClick page</a> describes saved details used for email and SMS signup. Rehearse a mobile signup, an email-only signup and an existing subscriber returning through the same offer. Record the disclosure, channel choice, destination profile and single welcome enrollment. The replacement must not treat an autofilled phone or email as permission for every channel.</p>
<h3>A cleaned SMS contact is imported as active</h3>
<p>The <a href="https://help.recart.com/en/articles/automated-list-cleaning">list-cleaning guide</a> distinguishes SMS subscription changes from other profile state. Include a suppressed SMS profile with valid email permission in the handoff fixture. Inspect both destination statuses and a blocked SMS enrollment. A full profile import must not undo the channel-specific exclusion or unnecessarily erase valid email permission.</p>
<h3>A managed campaign has no operator after cancellation</h3>
<p>Take a pending holiday campaign through creative approval, audience selection and scheduling with the new team. Require the approval record, named emergency-pause owner and a preview of exclusions. Include a recent purchaser and a customer already in a recovery flow. If the new supplier only supplies software, assign internal time or separately contract the missing work before ending the old service.</p>
<h3>The old popup and the new sender both welcome the shopper</h3>
<p>Use desktop and mobile fixtures, including a shopper switching devices. Record which collector creates the profile and which system owns the welcome offer. Inspect both queues after signup. Keep one enrollment owner, reconcile duplicate submissions with stable store/customer identifiers, and confirm the offered code works once under the intended Shopify combination rules.</p>
<h3>A number moves but customer replies do not reach support</h3>
<p>Confirm number type, release requirements, receiving registration and the agreed transfer window with both providers. Before closing old access, send a question and an opt-out from a test handset and inspect the receiving inbox and suppressed state. Export unresolved conversations or assign a manual handoff where needed; migrating contacts does not establish conversation continuity.</p>
<h3>An order arrives between email and the queued text</h3>
<p>Queue both channels, place a test order and then replay the original checkout event. Save the order ID, cancellation decision and replay record in each system. Withdrawal of SMS permission must independently block the text. Treat ambiguous identity matches as held work; shared email addresses are insufficient evidence to merge two customers’ phones or carts.</p>
<h2>Cart economics and useful recovery fixtures</h2>
<p>These are proposed evaluation exercises, not merchant results. The retained $668 basket at 32% gross margin has goods cost of $454.24. Full-price gross profit is $213.76. A 14% code removes $93.52 from revenue, leaving $574.48 revenue and $120.24 gross profit with goods cost fixed. Include messaging, service, shipping, payment and return costs separately. This large loss is a reason to inspect the objection, not an arbitrary rule that every cart above a value must switch suppliers.</p>
<p>For an out-of-stock variant, confirm that the restored cart does not promise unavailable goods; show an available option only with the shopper’s choice. For a shipping objection, display the current destination total rather than hiding it behind a code. For a gift-size question, route the reply to someone who can answer before the next reminder. Acceptance evidence is respectively inventory and restored cart, actual checkout totals, and the answered conversation with the next-send decision.</p>
<p>Retain bundle and coupon fixtures: a welcome discount plus a recovery offer must produce the intended Shopify total, including quantity and subscription changes. For minimum order quantities, validate the permitted quantity instead of applying a coupon that cannot complete checkout. For a mobile or BNPL interruption, verify the return link reaches the right live checkout and payment choices; do not promise financing approval. Test a repeat buyer separately so a recent purchase does not receive acquisition copy.</p>
<h2>Cut over the operating service, then assess value</h2>
<p>Freeze old enrollment, reconcile scheduled campaigns and delayed automations, and record a single owner for every pending action. Recheck current purchase, stock and permission at send time. Use a store-scoped event ledger to avoid duplicate or out-of-order replays. A rollback must cancel replacement work before restoring eligible old work; it must not revive withdrawn permission.</p>
<p>Compare the receiving proposal with the current invoice using the same SMS/MMS mix, destinations, capture scope, carrier charges, commitment and operator hours. Keep attribution definitions beside each report and reconcile orders by ID; click-attributed revenue alone does not prove additional profit. If testing incremental value, predeclare an eligible holdout and observation period appropriate to the store’s volume and buying cycle. Retain Recart when the actual capture and managed workflow justify the cost and the replacement cannot yet perform the required handoffs.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="FAQ: replacing Recart" />
</section>
</BaseLayout>
